### VendorBridge Approval Workflow API Tests
### Use REST Client extension in VS Code to run these tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@procurementToken = YOUR_PROCUREMENT_TOKEN_HERE
@manager1Token = YOUR_MANAGER1_TOKEN_HERE
@manager2Token = YOUR_MANAGER2_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Login as Procurement Officer (Sarah)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sarah.procurement@vendorbridge.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login as Manager 1 (Mike - Procurement Head)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mike.manager@vendorbridge.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Login as Manager 2 (Linda - Finance Approver)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "linda.finance@vendorbridge.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. List all submitted quotations for an RFQ (as Procurement Officer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quotations?rfq_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 5. Select a quotation (creates 2-level approval chain)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/quotations/1/select
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 6. List all approvals (as Manager 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{manager1Token}}

### 7. Get approval detail (as Manager 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals/1
Authorization: Bearer {{manager1Token}}

### 8. Approve Level 1 (as Manager 1 - Mike)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/approvals/1/action
Authorization: Bearer {{manager1Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "approved",
  "remarks": "Pricing is competitive and meets our requirements. Vendor has good track record."
}

### 9. List approvals (as Manager 2 - Linda)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{manager2Token}}

### 10. Get approval detail for Level 2 (as Manager 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals/2
Authorization: Bearer {{manager2Token}}

### 11. Approve Level 2 (as Manager 2 - Linda)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/approvals/2/action
Authorization: Bearer {{manager2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "approved",
  "remarks": "Budget approved. Proceed with purchase order creation."
}

### 12. Verify quotation is ready for PO (check approval chain)
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals/1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 13. REJECTION FLOW - Reject at Level 1
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/approvals/3/action
Authorization: Bearer {{manager1Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "rejected",
  "remarks": "Pricing exceeds budget. Need to renegotiate or select alternative vendor."
}

### 14. Filter approvals by RFQ
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals?rfq_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 15. View all completed approvals
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals?status=approved
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 16. View all rejected approvals
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals?status=rejected
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
